bids.description:
Hi there,

I'd like to apply for this sourcing project. I'm a China-based procurement agent with solid cross-border sourcing experience, familiar with the Yiwu, Ningbo and Shenzhen supplier networks — the key toy-manufacturing hubs.

What I'll deliver:

1. A shortlist of at least 3 verified factories already making paddle-and-ball / racket-style toys, with specs, MOQ, lead time and initial quotes;
2. Sample orders arranged and dispatched to your address, with materials/workmanship variations documented in photos and notes;
3. A basic factory audit (remote or in-person) covering production capability, ASTM F963 / EN-71 compliance and export history;
4. Payment terms, packaging and shipping negotiated, with a landed-cost breakdown to your nearest seaport;
5. Clear, documented communication with the supplier through order confirmation, so you can move straight to mass production once samples pass.

I can also arrange third-party QC as an add-on if you'd like an independent inspection layer.

Everything — factory details, price comparisons, audit findings — is shared transparently in fluent English at every step.

To start, please share your target budget, expected volumes and nearest seaport, and I'll confirm the timeline and fee structure. Looking forward to working with you.
